ng.com/store/Crusader-Castles-of-the-Teutonic-Knights-%282%29_9781841767123\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.ospreypublishing.com/img/osprey-mobile.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ospreypublishing.com/store/Crusader-Castles-of-the-Teutonic-Knights-%282%29_9781841767123\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Page: Page not found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.ospreypublishing.com/store/Crusader-Castles-of-the-Teutonic-Knights-%282%29_9781841767123\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.ospreypublishing.com/store/Crusader-Castles-of-the-Teutonic-Knights-%282%29_9781841767123 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Sorry, we couldn't find that page. Please visit our homepage https://ospreypublishing.com </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Two last ones i my favored, becouse of pictures of castles and cities you can use for your games as location guides.<br /> Also gives more info about domains where you would run Dark Ages setting games based on Livonia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","name":"Lachplesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T06:57:03-07:00","id":222082,"title":"","content":"Hello!<br /> Wish to share this handy map of Wenden i use for chronicle. Should give you quick insight.<br /> Once the most important castle of the Livonian Order (autonomous branch of Teutonic Order), it was the official residence for the Masters of the order.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/15mPUXK.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> This settlement was located near major trade routes from west to east and dominated the regional countryside.<br /> German crusaders known as the Livonian Brothers of the Sword began construction of a castle Wenden near the hill fort in 1209.<br /> In 1577, during the Livonian War, the garrison destroyed the castle to prevent it from falling into the control of Ivan the Terrible,<br /> who was decisively defeated in the Battle of Wenden (1578).<br /> <br /> A place for your need! Hall of Order Master.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.ambermarks.com/Atteli/Skanetie/Cesu%20raj/Cesis/Cesu-Pils-mestra-zale-RGuleke-1896.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The Livonian Master like the grandmaster of the Teutonic Order was elected by his fellow knights for a lifetime term.<br /> The grandmaster exercised supervisory powers and his advice was considered equal to a command.<br /> The grandmaster of Teutonic knights did not limit local autonomy, he rarely visited Livonia or sent ambassadors for oversight.<br /> <br /> Some inspirational Maters of Livonian Order:<br /> <span style=\"color:#2D5DA1\">\u25cf</span> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermann_Balk\" target=\"_blank\">Hermann Balk</a> 1237\u201338<br /> Dietrich von Gr\u00fcningen 1238\u201342<br /> Unknown authority ? 1242 The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_the_Ice\" target=\"_blank\">Battle of the Ice</a>, 20 Knights killed, 6 captured.<br /> Dietrich von Gr\u00fcningen 1244\u201346 <a href=\"http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dietrich_von_Gr%C3%BCningen#mediaviewer/Datei:Dundagas_pils_stela.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dietric...pils_stela.jpg</a><br /> Dietrich of Green Ingen entered the Order very young. However Gr\u00fcningen may have already acted as deputy of Balks in Livonia.<br /> Already in 1238, when Balk had left the country due to serious illness and because of serious disputes with the Bishop of Riga, Nicholas of Nauen, about the sovereign rights on the territory of the former Livonian Order, Dietrich followed by green rings as country champion in Livonia.<br /> Gr\u00fcningen remained until 1251 country champion in Livonia. From 1246 to 1259 he was also Landmeister of Prussia, where he followed Poppo of Osterna (1244-1246). From 1254 to 1256 he was under the Grand Master of Poppo Osterna in personal union both Landmeister of Prussia and German masters. Gr\u00fcningen completed the conquest of Courland and built a number of castles like (Kuld\u012bga) and Amboten (Emb\u016bte).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","user":"Lachplesis","date":". 08-08-2014, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","name":"Lachplesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T07:05:49-07:00","id":222092,"title":"","content":"I will nitpick, but I come from former Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Extreme spice here is a fact, that this region is the last Pagan stronghold in europe. </div> </div> </div>Last stronghold is relative, after all Grand Duchy was in 80 % Christian Orthodox, and part of Lithuanian elite converted to Eastern Christianity before Jogaila made a deal with Kingdom of Poland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Lithuanians annihilated crusaders Swordbrother order and later with the help of Poland destroyed Teutonic order. In this we can see long forged and eventual victory.) </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, Teutonic Order reorganised itself as Duchy of Prussia, and Lithuanians were main factor from stopping Kingdom of Poland from just annexing their lands. Lithuanians wanted weaker Teutonic Order as a vassal and did not want Poland to get stronger. We see how foolish and shortsighted it was, as subjects of Teutonic Order were eager to get annexed seeing what priviledges Royal Prussia got from seceding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T22:06:49-07:00","id":224858,"title":"","content":"Thnx for nitpicks Katsura!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Last stronghold is relative, after all Grand Duchy was in 80 % Christian Orthodox, and part of Lithuanian elite converted to Eastern Christianity before Jogaila made a deal with Kingdom of Poland. </div> </div> </div>Dark Ages setting is set in year 1230 wich is really nice number and DA:V20 will be set in 1242. Around this time majority of Lithuania is pagan.<br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Lithuania_%281219%E2%80%9395%29\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History...%E2%80%9395%29</a><br /> (Or at any time for game purpose it can be virtualy last wooden castle with rebelious veteran pagans in remote area with any supernatural as leader.)<br /> <br /> More than hundred years later when Jogaila made a deal with Kingdom of Poland 1380-1400 majority of Lithuanian elite cold be converted to Eastern Christianity or Roman Catholic. But most of the country all around Livonia and Lithuania still is pagan. People continued to worship their old gods in secret. Rebellions would spring out continuously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not exactly, Teutonic Order reorganised itself as Duchy of Prussia, and Lithuanians were main factor from stopping Kingdom of Poland from just annexing their lands. Lithuanians wanted weaker Teutonic Order as a vassal and did not want Poland to get stronger. We see how foolish and shortsighted it was, as subjects of Teutonic Order were eager to get annexed seeing what priviledges Royal Prussia got from seceding. </div> </div> </div>Yes, i agree. Will research more! Thnx again! CHeers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","user":"Lachplesis","date":". 08-11-2014, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2148-lachplesis","name":"Lachplesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T03:47:08-07:00","id":224967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dark Ages setting is set in year 1230 wich is really nice number and DA:V20 will be set in 1242. Around this time majority of Lithuania is pagan. </div> </div> </div>This also when Mindaugas began to encroach on Russian lands, and flirting with Western Christianity for political gain (briefly converted in 1250s). Needless to say, it is beginning of the process that formed the Lithuania of Jogaila, and interesting times as pagans are subjected to influences from other religions. You could put some emphasis on the time that is the time of change and uncertainty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rebellions would spring out continuously. </div> </div> </div>If you mean times after Jogaila's baptism, I don't remember any uprising except in those Lithuanian lands already seized by Teutonic Order. Jogaila did not have such zealous attitude as some neophyte rulers to provoke outright uprisings, but I'll research that.<br /> <br /> PS. No info I could find on post-1386 uprisings, but Pagan worship among folk people still persisted as far as in 1587 as one bishop complained in a letter that some his subjects don't even know what Christianity is. Rulers did ban worship and closed down blatant religious sites, but they little did to enforce that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:30:28-07:00","id":559851,"title":"","content":"I felt joy when I saw this post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As a GDL historian, it brought me joy to see people who are interested both in this field and WoD made me cry in joy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Influence of Cuci Ulus (Golden Horde) was also an important factor in GDL in high and late medieval period. Unfortunately it is not researched enough or at least not in the west. We know Tatar envoys in Gediminas time from the reports of papal envoys. So any members of middle eastern splats which are from Bulgar-Cuci Ulus is more possibility than an Arabia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6523-dzyhanas","name":"Dzyhanas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T11:05:52-07:00","id":568181,"title":"","content":"Lachlesis praise and thanks aren't enough for your work and willingness to share with us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Even as an European myself, eastern Europe is always less known and mysterious, especially because it's hardly studied unless one specializes in that field. It's great to have resources to use.<br /> <br /> From what I see it shows it's a work in progress, but I want to leave the suggestion to turn it into a PDF (possibly watermarked so you are always given credit) because it's important and valuable enough to become a sourcebook <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}